1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:07,600
BBNaija Season 11 — free fan polls in, win probabilities out.
No paid services. No X/Twitter API. Runs on a laptop.

2
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:12,600
Every week the engine reads free fan polls. The bbnaijadaily vote
widget is the primary full-share source — graded A.

3
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:17,200
Hand-logged Facebook polls are graded B. Official bottom-N reports
are grade A.

4
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:19,800
The C-grade titles never become shares — they only constrain
who finished top two.

5
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:24,600
Every observation becomes one row in a long matrix — and only the
last three weeks of rows are kept.

6
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:29,700
Rows covering fewer than two eligible actives are dropped.
Gambit housemates never enter the matrix at all.

7
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:33,900
Missing weeks are never invented — a gap is a no-op,
flagged in the run record.

8
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:37,700
Names resolve against a canonical roster: aliases are quarantined,
never dropped.

9
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:42,500
Each row is weighted by its source grade, its capped sample size,
and a recency decay.

10
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:46,800
Lambda is 0.6 per week — last week's poll counts more.
The 5,000 cap tames the widget's 600,000 votes.

11
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:51,600
Now the step that matters most: each row is renormalised over
the housemates it actually covers.

12
00:00:51,900 --> 00:00:55,700
So a three-name ballot is read as a three-name poll,
not as a landslide over the whole house.

13
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:59,900
Those row shares combine into one weighted share per housemate —
full-share rows only.

14
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:04,700
No Bayesian sampler, no blog-CPI:
the polls are the likelihood.

15
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:08,900
Anyone the polls did not cover inherits last week's share,
and is flagged as carried.

16
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:12,700
Never measured at all? The lowest measured share, as a floor,
and an unmeasured flag.

17
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:17,700
Official bottom-N and top-N reports then cap and floor shares,
with epsilon one percent.

18
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:22,700
Agree with the polls and they apply in full; fight them and the
share moves only halfway.

19
00:01:23,300 --> 00:01:27,500
Uncertainty comes from 1,000 seeded replicates,
resampling on two layers.

20
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:33,700
Rows are resampled by weight — between-poll disagreement —
then each poll's voters are redrawn.

21
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:38,500
The replicates give the 89% interval, the rank chips and the
podium — the same thousand draws.

22
00:01:38,800 --> 00:01:43,700
So does the head-to-head: the share of replicates where\nA finishes above B.

23
00:01:44,300 --> 00:01:48,500
Here is the whole model in one line: the aggregated share
is the win probability.

24
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:52,700
No softmax, no Dirichlet layer, no momentum tilt\nstacked on top of the tally.

25
00:01:53,300 --> 00:01:57,700
And every week is scored afterwards against what happened —
a Brier score on the eviction call.

26
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,700
Plus concordance between the poll order and the model's,\nand a tombstone when nothing was published.

27
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:06,000
Now the live board. The engine's call to win is Sheba —
25.3% aggregated share, and 95% to finish first.

28
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:09,700
Podium: Sheba, Temi Nkem, Ricky. Runner-up cards show P(top-3),
not the same number twice.

29
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:14,000
The trajectory chart plots aggregated share per week,
with 89% bootstrap bands.

30
00:02:14,300 --> 00:02:18,000
Hover any point for the exact share and its interval.

31
00:02:18,300 --> 00:02:22,000
This is the week control — the x-axis stops at week 10,\nbecause there is no week 11.

32
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:25,700
Step back to week 9 and every line, marker and tooltip
re-scopes to that week.

33
00:02:26,300 --> 00:02:29,800
Rank probabilities for every active housemate — P(number one),
P(top-3), P(top-5) — plus week-over-week momentum.

34
00:02:30,100 --> 00:02:32,800
Head-to-head compares any two: the win-probability difference
and the likely winner.

35
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:38,700
Code, data and methodology are all public — one week scored,\nBrier 0.043, concordance one half. Fan forecast, not official.
